## Tower Crane In Use

This project opts into reusable Claude Code tooling from the Tower Crane hub, referenced live
(float-on-HEAD) rather than copied — an update ratified in the hub reaches this project the next
time it runs, for everything Tower Crane manages in this file. This machine's copy of the hub
lives wherever `.claude/hub_pointer.md` (this project's own gitignored, per-host pointer file)
currently records — see that file's `shared_root:` value for the real path, or the hub's own
`MENU.md` there for the full catalog. Do not edit the shared files directly; to report a bug or
request an improvement, follow the filing protocol below. Tower Crane keeps everything it manages
in this file directive-only, with narrative in `README.md` and a decisions/activity log in
`project_progress.md` if this project uses them — its own convention for its own content, not a
requirement for the rest of this file.

Whether this file is actually live on **this** machine right now is decided by one thing: does
`.claude/hub_pointer.md` (gitignored, per-host, never itself tracked — regenerated by `"connect
project"`/`relocate.py`) exist? If it does, read it for the real hub path and this machine's host
identity, and everything below applies. If it doesn't, Tower Crane is not connected on this
machine, full stop — none of the host-specific behavior below applies, and there is no need (and
no reliable way) to determine which machine this is instead. Don't guess.

If it does exist but the Shared Workflow Protocol below didn't load (no `resume` procedure is
available to you — usually the CLAUDE.md import-approval dialog was declined or never shown), run
`python "<shared_root>/scripts/readiness.py" --project-root .` (`shared_root:` from
`hub_pointer.md`) and report what it lists to the user.

If it doesn't exist, the following may still be present on disk (left behind, or live for a
*different* connected host sharing this same repo) but are inert here — ignore them, don't try to
use or explain them: everything under `.claude/skills/`, `.claude/hooks/_hub_dispatch.py`, any
`.claude/settings.json` hook entry invoking `_hub_dispatch.py` plus its `Read(...)` permission
line, and the `@import`/`@.claude/hub_pointer.md` line at the top of this file.

